('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000087', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'You can fix ChatGPT in 5 days. Everyone says to double down on prompting from scratch, and that is exactly backwards. When I switched, my results went from nothing to a usable draft in 5 weeks. Step one, audit ChatGPT. Step two, cut prompting from scratch. Step three, track it for 5 days. For example, a friend tried this last month and got a usable draft without changing anything else. Side note, this works even if you hate prompting from scratch.', 'en', 'whisper-1', 58, 'ok'),
('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000088', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'time blocking is a scam and everyone is doing it anyway. Quick context: I have been doing this for years and I kept getting it wrong. When I switched, my results went from nothing to a calm week in 3 weeks. For example, a friend tried this last month and got a calm week without changing anything else. Save this so you actually try it, and follow for part two. Side note, this works even if you hate time blocking.', 'en', 'whisper-1', 73, 'ok'),
('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000089', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'posting daily is the single fastest path to ten thousand views. The problem is that most advice ignores how your hook actually behaves. When I switched, my results went from nothing to ten thousand views in 7 weeks. Do this and ten thousand views stops being a goal and becomes your baseline. Save this so you actually try it, and follow for part two.', 'en', 'whisper-1', 63, 'ok'),
('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000090', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'What if skipping breakfast is the reason you never get stable energy? The problem is that most advice ignores how your sleep actually behaves. Side note, this works even if you hate skipping breakfast.', 'en', 'whisper-1', 48, 'ok'),
('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000091', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'You can fix your to-do list in 3 days. The problem is that most advice ignores how your to-do list actually behaves. Everyone says to double down on time blocking, and that is exactly backwards. Do this and a calm week stops being a goal and becomes your baseline.', 'en', 'whisper-1', 23, 'ok'),
